  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "How many integers from 1 to 210 are:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p32-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "divisible by 3 or 7",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$90$",
          "worked": "Let $A$ and $B$ be the sets of integers from 1 to 210 divisible by 3 and 7, respectively. Their intersection consists of multiples of 21.\n$$\\begin{align*}|A|&=210\\div3=70\\\\|B|&=210\\div7=30\\\\|A\\cap B|&=210\\div21=10\\\\|A\\cup B|&=|A|+|B|-|A\\cap B|\\\\|A\\cup B|&=70+30-10\\\\|A\\cup B|&=90\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "not divisible by 3 or 7?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$120$",
          "worked": "From part (a), 90 integers are divisible by 3 or 7. Subtract these from the 210 integers.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=210-|A\\cup B|\\\\N&=210-90\\\\N&=120\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
